{
  "id": "2026-09-14-suggestions-view-initialization-api",
  "scope": "suggestions",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "question": "Is EditorRoot authored the best durable API for initializing suggesting mode, or should SuggestionPlugin configuration own it?",
  "model": "GPT-5 / Codex; exact model variant unavailable",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2 with redesign-from-first-principles",
  "trigger": "The user requested a fresh harsh honest review after implementation and specifically challenged whether the selected initialization API is best.",
  "requirements": [
    "Initialize intent and projection before the first rendered frame without replay, an effect, or duplicated mutable state.",
    "Keep the policy local to one mounted view so sibling views over the same document may differ and toolbar commands update only their view.",
    "Keep generic Plate editor components independent of the optional SuggestionPlugin while preserving capability inference.",
    "Load authored suggestions as part of the canonical document and comments as independent application records."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reaffirms the prior initialization review after rechecking the implemented Plate-to-Plite forwarding, native EditorRoot ownership, SuggestionPlugin runtime mode API, the real editor-ai consumer, the earlier Plite view-ownership decision and the settled execution receipt. Unlike the prior proposal-only review, the target now has focused lifetime and browser proof. Those existing commands were not rerun for this source reassessment.",
  "summary": "Stop moving initialization into SuggestionPlugin configuration. Keep EditorRoot authored: it is the only compared contract that initializes the exact native view before render without global plugin state, hidden precedence, late effects or another wrapper vocabulary.",
  "verdict": "stop",
  "previous": "2026-09-14-suggestions-initialization",
  "relation": "reaffirms",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep EditorRoot authored: selected. The root already owns readOnly, root selection, decorations and callbacks for one mounted view; the authored policy is another native view input and is conditionally available only when the editor installs authored capability.",
    "Configure SuggestionPlugin initialState or options with mode suggesting: rejected. Plugin construction is editor-wide while intent and projection are mutable per-view facts. Making configuration a default introduces override precedence and still needs the root to own the actual state.",
    "Have SuggestionPlugin apply its configured mode from a provider or effect: rejected. The native view already exists by then, so this restores late coordination and risks an incorrect first frame or resetting a user-selected mode.",
    "Add a generic plugin-to-view initialization contribution: rejected for this job. It creates conflict resolution, ordering and lifecycle machinery so one optional plugin can indirectly set one existing native prop.",
    "Add SuggestionRoot, SuggestionView, or a suggestionMode helper: rejected. A wrapper duplicates EditorRoot's mounted lifetime; a helper only renames the explicit intent/projection value while leaving the same owner and adding public vocabulary.",
    "Move the policy to useCreateEditor or the persisted document: rejected. One document can have simultaneous accepted, proposed and markup views; persisting or editor-owning the choice destroys that independence.",
    "Rename or nest the prop under view: rejected. EditorRoot is already the view boundary and its root, readOnly and authored props are the native EditorViewOptions. A view object adds nesting without changing ownership or removing coordination."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "This is a bounded API and ownership reassessment, not a new runtime execution. Matching implementation evidence records 20 Chromium suggestion journeys, focused view-lifetime contracts, full www typechecking and installed editor builds. Those receipts prove the implemented behavior, not performance or complete Google Docs parity. The full Plate type-contract suite still has the separately recorded table TS2589 limitation.",
